repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/Breakthrough-problems-1"
keywords:
  - tournament
  - Hamilton cycle
  - random blow-up
  - Hessian determinant
  - skew-symmetric matrix
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  For a regular tournament on d vertices with skew adjacency matrix S, the Hessian determinant H
  that Wormald attached to its random blow-ups equals d det(d^2 I + S^2)/det(d^2 I - S^2). Hence
  H is nonzero and d/H is the square of a rational number, as Wormald conjectured. For the cyclic
  tournament the formula gives sqrt(d/H) = ((d+1)^d + (d-1)^d)/((d+i)^d + (d-i)^d), so the
  associated constants tend to cosh 1/cos 1 = 2.8559578925..., which proves a second conjecture of
  Wormald and identifies his numerical constant. The algebra is formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib.
